property below, quote the exact line(s) it rests on:

- libc series: leaked-address offset arithmetic (`libc.address = leak - <off>`),
  `one_gadget` constants, `__free_hook`/`__malloc_hook`/`main_arena` offsets, or
  a `libc.so.6` the solver `LD_PRELOAD`s. A matching offset pins the glibc minor
  version — cite the constant, do not guess.
- loader + architecture: the supplied binary's ELF header and `PT_INTERP`
  (attachments), cross-checked against the exploit's `p64`/`p32` packing.
- protections the exploit RELIES ON: `NX` (ROP/ret2libc, not stack shellcode),
  `PIE` off (hardcoded .text/PLT) or on (leak-relative), a canary leak/bypass,
  partial-RELRO GOT overwrite, CET/`endbr` notes. Set exactly what the exploit
  assumes; cite the line.

Select the catalog bundle (`instance_data.pwn_runtime`, cache
`{{ instance_data.pwn_runtime.status }}`) whose glibc series matches the pinned
offsets, or the solver-shipped libc/loader pair; never cross a libc and loader
from different bundles. Record the selection and every citation in the
`pwn_runtime` object (schema in the category section) with `confidence: inferred`
