## Realize it as a Dockerfile

Author a Dockerfile installing the inferred libc/loader pair and preserving the
binary's interpreter, arch, permissions, and the exact hardening the exploit
needs, served over the declared protocol. Do NOT weaken a protection to ease
later exploitation — fidelity first; the exploit adapts to the runtime.

## When the exploit anchors no runtime

If the exploit hardcodes no libc offset, ships no libc, and asserts no
protection you can tie to a line, do not invent a glibc minor version. Emit
`status: blocked` with a `runtime_inference_unsupported` blocker citing what the
exploit does and does not reveal; `next_action`: supply a libc/loader or writeup.

